<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Utah</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Utah is a state in the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, with its capital at Salt Lake City. Settled from 1847 by members of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-jesus-christ-of-latter-day-saints">Church of Jesus Christ of Latter-day Saints</a> led by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigham-young">Brigham Young</a>, it was organised as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah-territory">Utah Territory</a> in 1850 after the Mormons' proposed State of Deseret was rejected. Conflict with the federal government over polygamy delayed statehood until 1896, and the church remains central to its life.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/utah.jpg" alt="Utah" width="320" height="192" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The State of Utah · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Utah.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
